Step 1: Prepare all nodes
Update the system
sudo apt update
sudo apt upgrade -y

Set the hostname.

Master:

sudo hostnamectl set-hostname k8s-master

Worker1:

sudo hostnamectl set-hostname k8s-worker01

Worker2:

sudo hostnamectl set-hostname k8s-worker02

Update /etc/hosts on all nodes.

sudo vi /etc/hosts

Example:

172.31.30.35    k8s-master
172.31.23.30    k8s-worker01
172.31.20.15    k8s-worker02
Step 2: Disable Swap
sudo swapoff -a

Disable swap permanently.

sudo sed -i '/ swap / s/^/#/' /etc/fstab

Verify:

free -h

Swap should be:

Swap: 0B
Step 3: Enable Kernel Modules
cat <<EOF | sudo tee /etc/modules-load.d/k8s.conf
overlay
br_netfilter
EOF

Load modules.

sudo modprobe overlay
sudo modprobe br_netfilter
Step 4: Configure sysctl
cat <<EOF | sudo tee /etc/sysctl.d/k8s.conf
net.bridge.bridge-nf-call-iptables=1
net.bridge.bridge-nf-call-ip6tables=1
net.ipv4.ip_forward=1
EOF

Apply:

sudo sysctl --system

Verify:

sysctl net.ipv4.ip_forward

Expected:

net.ipv4.ip_forward = 1
Step 5: Install Containerd
sudo apt install -y containerd

Create configuration.

sudo mkdir -p /etc/containerd

Generate default config.

containerd config default | sudo tee /etc/containerd/config.toml

Enable Systemd cgroup.

sudo sed -i 's/SystemdCgroup = false/SystemdCgroup = true/' \
/etc/containerd/config.toml

Restart.

sudo systemctl restart containerd
sudo systemctl enable containerd

Verify.

sudo systemctl status containerd
Step 6: Install Kubernetes Packages

Install prerequisites.

sudo apt install -y apt-transport-https ca-certificates curl gpg

Create keyring.

sudo mkdir -p /etc/apt/keyrings

Download GPG key.

curl -fsSL https://pkgs.k8s.io/core:/stable:/v1.33/deb/Release.key \
| sudo gpg --dearmor -o /etc/apt/keyrings/kubernetes-apt-keyring.gpg

Add repository.

echo "deb [signed-by=/etc/apt/keyrings/kubernetes-apt-keyring.gpg] \
https://pkgs.k8s.io/core:/stable:/v1.33/deb/ /" \
| sudo tee /etc/apt/sources.list.d/kubernetes.list

Update.

sudo apt update

Install packages.

sudo apt install -y kubelet kubeadm kubectl

Prevent upgrades.

sudo apt-mark hold kubelet kubeadm kubectl

Verify.

kubectl version --client
Step 7: Initialize the Master

Run only on the master.

sudo kubeadm init \
--pod-network-cidr=192.168.0.0/16

At the end you'll receive a join command.

Example:

kubeadm join <MASTER-IP>:6443 \
--token <TOKEN> \
--discovery-token-ca-cert-hash sha256:<HASH>

Save it.

Step 8: Configure kubectl
mkdir -p $HOME/.kube
sudo cp /etc/kubernetes/admin.conf $HOME/.kube/config
sudo chown $(id -u):$(id -g) $HOME/.kube/config

Verify.

kubectl get nodes

Initially:

k8s-master   NotReady

This is expected until a CNI plugin is installed.

Step 9: Install Calico

Apply the official manifest (using a stable release rather than a development master image):

kubectl apply -f https://raw.githubusercontent.com/projectcalico/calico/v3.30.2/manifests/calico.yaml

Wait.

kubectl get pods -n kube-system

Verify.

kubectl get nodes

Expected:

k8s-master   Ready
Step 10: Join Worker Nodes

Run the kubeadm join command generated during initialization on each worker.

Example:

sudo kubeadm join <MASTER-IP>:6443 \
--token <TOKEN> \
--discovery-token-ca-cert-hash sha256:<HASH>

Check:

kubectl get nodes

Expected:

NAME            STATUS
k8s-master      Ready
k8s-worker01    Ready
k8s-worker02    Ready
Step 11: Remove the Control Plane Taint (Optional)

For lab environments:

kubectl taint nodes k8s-master node-role.kubernetes.io/control-plane:NoSchedule-
Step 12: Verify Cluster
kubectl cluster-info
kubectl get componentstatuses
kubectl get pods -A
